.build/
.swiftpm/
*.xcodeproj
!SuperSubmitter.xcodeproj/
!SuperSubmitter.xcodeproj/**
# Per-user Xcode state. XcodeGen writes the rest of the project from project.yml.
**/xcuserdata/
.DS_Store
.super-submitter/

# The Aptabase app key is a real credential, and the names of the
# variables around it are nobody's business either. Both files stay local.
.env
.env.example

# The same key again, in the form the Xcode build reads: `.env` reaches
# `swift run` and nothing else, so a bundle needs its own copy. Only the local
# file is ignored. Analytics.xcconfig itself is tracked and holds no key,
# because XcodeGen refuses to generate the project when a file named under
# `configFiles` is missing, and a clone has to be able to build.
Supporting/Analytics.local.xcconfig

# Working folders that describe the product rather than build it. They stay on
# the machine that writes them; the public tree shows the app and nothing else.
.claude/
.design-notes/

# The release runbook and its rendering. It names the signing certificate, the
# team, and the shape of every secret the workflow reads, which is a map of the
# release for anybody who wants one. It stays on the machine that ships.
RELEASING.html
RELEASING.pdf

# Icon Composer writes these from super-submitter-icon.icon on every export.
super-submitter-icon Exports/

# The 6,084-page App Store Connect API mirror under docs/ is a local-only
# reference corpus fetched from sosumi.ai. It regenerates on demand; it does
# not belong in history.
docs/

# The release workflow builds into this.
dist/

# Private keys. The Sign in with Apple .p8 downloads once and the signing
# certificate .p12 comes out of the Keychain, and both are easy to drop in
# here on the way to a password manager. Neither belongs in a commit.
*.p8
*.p12

# The specs, the plans, and the working notes at the root. They describe the
# product rather than build it, they change on their own schedule, and several
# carry service configuration that has no business in a repository. Nested
# Markdown stays, so the vendored skill references under .claude keep working.
/*.md
# The one exception: the front door of the public repository.
!/README.md

# Local helpers: one takes the website screenshots, one mints an Apple client
# secret. Neither is part of the build.
tools/*.sh
tools/*.swift

# tools/screenshots.sh regenerates every one of these from the app on demand,
# so the repository was carrying a few megabytes of build output.
design/screenshots/
